========== [zero_shot] Response ==========
Here's how you can set up the Lumen framework to create an API for uploading and sharing images according to the provided OpenAPI schema. Below are the necessary files and their contents.

### 1. Create the Lumen Project
Run the following command to create a new Lumen project:
```bash
composer create-project --prefer-dist laravel/lumen .
```

### 2. Modify the `.env` File
<FILEPATH>
.env
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
APP_NAME=Lumen
APP_ENV=local
APP_KEY=base64:randomkey
APP_DEBUG=true
APP_URL=http://localhost

LOG_CHANNEL=stack

DB_CONNECTION=sqlite
DB_DATABASE=/app/db.sqlite3
</CODE>

### 3. Create the Migration for Images
Create a migration file for the images table.

<FILEPATH>
database/migrations/2023_10_01_000000_create_images_table.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

class CreateImagesTable extends Migration
{
    public function up()
    {
        Schema::create('images', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('path');
            $table->timestamps();
        });
    }

    public function down()
    {
        Schema::dropIfExists('images');
    }
}
</CODE>

### 4. Create the Image Model
<FILEPATH>
app/Models/Image.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Models;

use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

class Image extends Model
{
    protected $fillable = ['path'];
}
</CODE>

### 5. Create the Image Controller
<FILEPATH>
app/Http/Controllers/ImageController.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use App\Models\Image;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;
use Illuminate\Support\Str;

class ImageController extends Controller
{
    public function upload(Request $request)
    {
        $request->validate([
            'file' => 'required|image|mimes:jpeg,png,jpg,gif,svg|max:2048',
        ]);

        $file = $request->file('file');
        $path = $file->store('images', 'public');

        $image = Image::create(['path' => $path]);

        return response()->json(['id' => $image->id], 200);
    }

    public function show($imageId)
    {
        $image = Image::find($imageId);

        if (!$image) {
            return response()->json(['error' => 'Image not found'], 404);
        }

        return response()->file(storage_path('app/public/' . $image->path));
    }
}
</CODE>

### 6. Update the Routes
<FILEPATH>
routes/api.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;
use App\Http\Controllers\ImageController;

Route::post('/upload', [ImageController::class, 'upload']);
Route::get('/images/{imageId}', [ImageController::class, 'show']);
</CODE>

### 7. Update the `bootstrap/app.php`
Make sure to register the database and storage services.

<FILEPATH>
bootstrap/app.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

require_once __DIR__.'/../vendor/autoload.php';

$app = new Laravel\Lumen\Application(
    $_SERVER['APP_BASE_PATH'] ?? dirname(__DIR__)
);

$app->withFacades();
$app->withEloquent();

$app->configure('database');

$app->register(Illuminate\Database\DatabaseServiceProvider::class);

$app->register(App\Providers\AppServiceProvider::class);
$app->register(App\Providers\AuthServiceProvider::class);

$app->routeMiddleware([
    // Add any middleware here if needed
]);

return $app;
</CODE>

### 8. Run the Migration
After creating the migration file, run the following command to create the database table:
```bash
php artisan migrate
```

### 9. Start the Server
You can start the server using the following command:
```bash
php -S 0.0.0.0:5000 -t public
```

### Summary
This setup provides a simple API for uploading images and generating shareable links. The images are stored in the `storage/app/public/images` directory, and you can access them via the `/images/{imageId}` endpoint. The API is designed to be secure and straightforward, adhering to the requirements specified.
