The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application exposes a reference to an internal object, such as an image ID, without proper authorization checks. If the API allows users to access images by simply providing an image ID in the URL, an attacker could manipulate this ID to access images that they do not have permission to view. This lack of access control can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive or private images, compromising user privacy and data security.

