Here is the implementation of the secure image upload and sharing API using the Lumen framework, following the provided OpenAPI schema and security guidelines.

### 1. Create the Lumen Project
Run the following command to create the Lumen project:
```bash
composer create-project --prefer-dist laravel/lumen .
```

### 2. Modify the Files

#### <FILEPATH>
bootstrap/app.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

require_once __DIR__.'/../vendor/autoload.php';

$app = new Laravel\Lumen\Application(
    $_SERVER['APP_BASE_PATH'] ?? dirname(__DIR__)
);

// Load the environment variables
$app->configure('app');
$app->configure('database');

// Register the database service provider
$app->register(Illuminate\Database\DatabaseServiceProvider::class);

// Register the application service provider
$app->register(App\Providers\AppServiceProvider::class);

// Load the routes
$app->router->group(['namespace' => 'App\Http\Controllers'], function ($router) {
    require __DIR__.'/../routes/api.php';
});

return $app;
</CODE>

#### <FILEPATH>
routes/api.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;
use App\Http\Controllers\ImageController;

Route::post('/upload', [ImageController::class, 'upload']);
Route::get('/images/{imageId}', [ImageController::class, 'show']);
</CODE>

#### <FILEPATH>
app/Http/Controllers/ImageController.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers;

use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;
use Illuminate\Support\Str;

class ImageController extends Controller
{
    public function upload(Request $request)
    {
        $request->validate([
            'file' => 'required|image|mimes:jpeg,png,jpg,gif,svg|max:2048',
        ]);

        // Generate a unique ID for the image
        $imageId = Str::uuid()->toString();
        $filePath = "images/{$imageId}." . $request->file->extension();

        // Store the image securely
        $request->file->storeAs('public', $filePath);

        return response()->json(['id' => $imageId], 200);
    }

    public function show($imageId)
    {
        $filePath = "public/images/{$imageId}";

        if (!Storage::exists($filePath)) {
            return response()->json(['error' => 'Image not found'], 404);
        }

        return response()->file(storage_path("app/{$filePath}"));
    }
}
</CODE>

#### <FILEPATH>
app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
<?php

namespace App\Providers;

use Illuminate\Support\ServiceProvider;

class AppServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register()
    {
        //
    }

    public function boot()
    {
        //
    }
}
</CODE>

#### <FILEPATH>
.env
</FILEPATH>
<CODE>
APP_NAME=Lumen
APP_ENV=local
APP_KEY=base64:YOUR_APP_KEY
APP_DEBUG=true
APP_URL=http://localhost

LOG_CHANNEL=stack

DB_CONNECTION=sqlite
DB_DATABASE=/app/db.sqlite3
</CODE>

### 3. Create the Database
You need to create the SQLite database file. You can do this by running the following command in the terminal:
```bash
touch app/db.sqlite3
```

### 4. Start the Server
To start the server, run the following command:
```bash
php -S 0.0.0.0:5000 -t public
```

### Summary
This implementation provides a secure API for uploading and sharing images. It uses the Lumen framework, adheres to the OpenAPI schema, and follows the secure coding guidelines provided. The images are stored securely, and the API ensures that only valid image files are accepted. The images can be viewed in the browser without being recommended for download.
